// The mannequins above stand on PLAYER CUTSCENE entity templates, and cutscene rigs
// ship almost no locomotion clips - that is the male glide, and it has been the male
// glide since the first session. Story NPCs carry COMPLETE locomotion sets on their
// own entities (RedSync corroborates: their remotes are literally Jackie and Panam,
// and their movement is the part that works). These two records are the muppet
// multiplayer manners - blank names so the server's name reaches the nameplate,
// NoReaction, crouch/sprint - applied over the story records WITHOUT overriding
// template or appearance, so the NPC's own rig and clips are what spawns.
//
// Deliberately NOT the defaults yet. Character.Panam spawns are proven (/npc);
// Character.Jackie is the unvalidated half - one -puppet-record session decides.
// TweakXL skips an unresolvable record and logs it, so a wrong Jackie name cannot
// take the file down with it.

Character.MaJackie : Character.Jackie {
	priority = "SpawnableObjectPriority.Regular";
	reactionPreset = "ReactionPresets.NoReaction";
	uiNameplate = "UINameplate.MpPlayerSettings";
	abilities += [ "Ability.CanCrouch", "Ability.CanSprint" ];
	displayName = "";
	fullDisplayName = "";
	alternativeDisplayName = "";
}

Character.WaPanam : Character.Panam {
	priority = "SpawnableObjectPriority.Regular";
	reactionPreset = "ReactionPresets.NoReaction";
	uiNameplate = "UINameplate.MpPlayerSettings";
	abilities += [ "Ability.CanCrouch", "Ability.CanSprint" ];
	displayName = "";
	fullDisplayName = "";
	alternativeDisplayName = "";
}
